<article class="env-lemma" id="0GLE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GLE">Lemma <span data-tag="0GLE">63.11.7</span>.</a> Consider a cartesian square </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X' \ar[r]_{g'} \ar[d]_{f'} &  X \ar[d]^ f \\  Y' \ar[r]^ g &  Y }  \]
</div>
  <p> of quasi-compact and quasi-separated schemes with $f$ separated and of finite type. Then we have $Rf^! \circ Rg_* = Rg'_* \circ R(f')^!$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By uniqueness of adjoint functors this follows from base change for derived lower shriek: we have $g^{-1} \circ Rf_! = Rf'_! \circ (g')^{-1}$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/0F7L" data-tag="0F7L">63.9.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>